{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Pinned upstream API evidence (2026-09-03)\n\nVerified directly against the python-hcl2 v8.1.3 tag:\n- `hcl2/api.py` imports `SerializationOptions` from `hcl2.utils`; `load`/`loads` accept `serialization_options` and pass it into serialization.\n- `hcl2/utils.py` defines the `SerializationOptions` dataclass, its `with_meta: bool = False` field, and the exact emitted metadata names `__start_line__` / `__end_line__`.\n- The pinned getting-started guide documents `SerializationOptions(with_meta=True)` with those exact keys.\n\nSources:\nhttps://github.com/amplify-education/python-hcl2/blob/v8.1.3/hcl2/api.py\nhttps://github.com/amplify-education/python-hcl2/blob/v8.1.3/hcl2/utils.py\nhttps://github.com/amplify-education/python-hcl2/blob/v8.1.3/docs/01_getting_started.md\n\nThe implementation tests still exercise the installed 8.1.3 package through the real parser boundary; this note establishes that the planned symbol, parameter, and key spellings are source-verified rather than recalled."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788475643015016781,"uuid":"e59c824b-c357-45bd-a170-0c5b80f7af08"}